(defsystem "harness-demos-music-theory"
  :version "0.5.1"
  :description "Demo of music-theory 0.5.1. MT0: spelled pitches parsed and printed in ASCII and Unicode, MIDI numbers and the scientific octave (B#3 and C4 are enharmonic, not equal), the line of fifths from Fbb to B##, intervals with quality, number, compound and simple forms, inversion and reversal, transposition with exact spelling (C major up an A4 is F# major), INVALID-PITCH and INVALID-INTERVAL with USE-VALUE restarts. MT1: meters (simple, compound, additive, C and C|) and their beats, the metric-weight hierarchy, dots and tuplets, tie splitting at barlines and strong beats, tempo conversion and phrase windows. MT2: keys and key signatures from Cb to C#, natural, harmonic and melodic minor scales, scale degrees and chromatic notes as altered degrees, Roman numerals (inversions, applied chords, the Neapolitan) to chords and back, mixture, and a I-vi-ii6-V7-I progression. MT3: chord symbols from a lead-sheet chart parsed into root, quality, extensions and alterations and realised as spelled tones, the classical, pop and jazz dialects (Cdim, C°, C-7, CΔ7, Cø, C7alt, C+) read and printed, a print-and-parse round-trip sweep, Unicode and ASCII accidentals and slash chords, essential tones for three or four voices, transposition by interval and by key, and CHORD-SYMBOL-PARSE-ERROR with its position, the SKIP-CHORD-SYMBOL and USE-VALUE restarts and the UNKNOWN-CHORD-QUALITY warning. MT4: MIDI numbers spelled by line-of-fifths rules S0-S7 with and without a key hint, per-note ambiguity, remote keys (C# and Db major), the AMBIGUOUS-SPELLING signal with USE-VALUE and MUFFLE-WARNING, pitch-class histograms and DETECT-KEY under the Krumhansl-Kessler, Temperley and Aarden profiles, TRANSPOSE-TO-KEY of a melody and its chord symbols, and CHOOSE-ENHARMONIC-KEY. 0.5.1: chromatic lines spelled as notated (music-theory#14: the issue rows before and after, and the 57-line chromatic corpus next to the 50 melodies), any integer octave in text (#15: random round trips over octaves -5..15), and chord symbols to MusicXML kind and degrees and back (#16)"
  :author "egao1980"
  :license "MIT"
  :depends-on ((:version "music-theory" "0.5.1"))
  :serial t
  :pathname "src"
  :components ((:file "package")
               (:file "demo")))
